From: Waltteri Hooli <1420194+wahooli@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] main: skip the 2-second cloud status poll when there is nothing to ask

The frontend calls emudeck("cloud_decky_check_status") every 2 s for as long
as Decky runs. Each call logged the full command line at INFO (into the
journal through the plugin loader) and rewrote ~/.config/EmuDeck/logs/decky.log
— about 43,000 of each a day, on flash.

On dev the bash ("LEGACY") backend is supported too, and there every poll would
source all of functions/all.sh. So: with no backend at all, every command
returns "" at once, as before; on the bash backend the poll returns "" while
cloud sync is off. A poll that does run no longer logs or rewrites decky.log;
every other command logs as before.

---
diff --git a/main.py b/main.py
index 1ed117e..aa99af2 100644
--- a/main.py
+++ b/main.py
@@ -125,14 +125,31 @@ class Plugin:
 
     async def emudeck(self, command):
 
+        # The UI polls cloud_decky_check_status every 2 s for as long as Decky
+        # runs. Without a backend there is nothing to run, and on the bash one
+        # each poll would source all of functions/all.sh: return before a
+        # subprocess, a log line and a decky.log rewrite when there is nothing
+        # to ask.
+        poll = command == "cloud_decky_check_status"
+        if get_mode() == "LEGACY":
+            if not (emudeck_backend / "functions" / "all.sh").exists():
+                return ""
+            if poll and read_legacy_settings().get("cloud_sync_status") is not True:
+                return ""
+
         bash_command = build_shell_command(command)
 
-        log(bash_command)
+        if not poll:
+            log(bash_command)
 
         result = subprocess.run(bash_command, shell=True, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, text=True)
 
         cleaned_stdout = result.stdout.strip()
 
+        # The status poll keeps decky.log as the last real command left it.
+        if poll:
+            return cleaned_stdout
+
         os.makedirs(emudeck_logs, exist_ok=True)
 
         # Escribir el resultado en un archivo de log
